    <!--
        ADDED 2026-08-25 (native LOI/PSA Details, scope addition). A section of its own holding
        ONE field: LOI__c.Selected_Offer__c, the link back to the
        Disposition_Offer__c row this LOI was raised against.

        WHY ITS OWN SECTION RATHER THAN APPENDED TO THE EXISTING ONE. It is not a negotiation
        term - it is a pointer to a different record - and dropping it in among the price and
        date fields invites it to be read as one. A one-field section reads as what it is: a
        way out of this record and into the offer.

        behavior = Readonly ON PURPOSE. The field is stamped by
        DispositionStageEntryService inside the same Database.insert that creates this record.
        Making it editable here would invite a hand-edit that silently disagrees with the
        disposition's own selected offer, with nothing to reconcile the two.
        ⚠ Readonly on the LAYOUT is a display choice, not a permission - DPEG_Disposition_Edit
        deliberately grants editable = true on this field so the one-off backfill (which runs in
        USER mode) is not refused. The two are not in conflict; they answer different questions.

        🔴 THIS LAYOUT IS SHARED WITH THE ACQUISITION RECORD TYPES, AND THE FIELD WILL RENDER
        BLANK FOR THEM, PERMANENTLY. An acquisition LOI hangs off Opportunity__c
        and has no Disposition__c, so it has no offers and there is nothing to link. THAT IS A
        VISIBILITY COST ONLY - no acquisition path, flow, validation rule or automation reads
        this field, and none was touched by the change that added it. If the empty section ever
        becomes a real annoyance the fix is record-type-specific layouts, which is a much larger
        change than this one and was deliberately not started here.
    -->
    <layoutSections>
        <customLabel>true</customLabel>
        <detailHeading>true</detailHeading>
        <editHeading>true</editHeading>
        <label>Disposition Offer</label>
        <layoutColumns>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Readonly</behavior>
                <field>Selected_Offer__c</field>
            </layoutItems>
        </layoutColumns>
        <style>OneColumn</style>
    </layoutSections>
    <layoutSections>
        <customLabel>true</customLabel>
        <detailHeading>false</detailHeading>
        <editHeading>false</editHeading>
        <label>Custom Links</label>
        <layoutColumns/>
        <layoutColumns/>
        <layoutColumns/>
        <style>CustomLinks</style>
    </layoutSections>
